# =============================================================================
# subFinder release — git ignore rules (push-ready)
# =============================================================================
#
# Anything excluded here is distributed via Google Drive zips. See README §5
# for download links and where to extract.
# Comments must be on their own line — inline comments break gitignore patterns.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Calibration .npz/.json files — distributed in-repo, no ignore needed.
# final_model.pkl is tracked via Git LFS (see .gitattributes); the pointer
# file is committed, the 173 MB blob lives on LFS storage.
# All 725 classifier.{joblib,keras} weights are committed directly:
#   - largest single file is 45 MB (under GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold)
#   - aggregate repo size ~8 GB (exceeds GitHub's 5 GB recommended cap; you
#     will get an email warning but pushes still succeed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Embeddings (May 2026 rewrite)
# Six global models in artifacts/embeddings/, ~38 MB total, all tracked in
# regular git — no LFS, no per-fold copies.
#
# What they replaced: artifacts/embeddings_cache/, which held one gensim model
# per (seed, fold, architecture, regime) — 300 models, 186 GB, of which ~186 GB
# was FastText n-gram hash tables (2.24 GB each, 0.55% of rows reachable).
# See scripts/01_train_embeddings.py for why the per-fold split was dropped.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/embeddings_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-trial classifier weights — NOT shipped (they were 6.4 GB across 625 fits).
# Everything downstream reads probs_test.npz / probs_train.npz / meta.json,
# which ARE tracked. Regenerate the weights with scripts/02 and scripts/03;
# see README "Reproducing the per-trial weights".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/predictions/*/*/classifier.joblib
artifacts/predictions/*/*/classifier.keras

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / build noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter / LaTeX noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.toc
paper/*.synctex.gz
paper/*.fdb_latexmk
paper/*.fls
paper/*.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release zips themselves (these live OUTSIDE the repo at /Users/ved/release_zips/)
# but listed here so they're never accidentally committed if someone moves them in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
release_zips/
# Exception: the 6 zipped unravel HTMLs that we DO ship in-repo because their
# raw forms exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit. Restore with
#   bash unravel/unzip_heavy.sh
!unravel/unravel_report.html.zip
!unravel/beta-glucan.html.zip
!unravel/host-glycan.html.zip
!unravel/v2/unravel_report.html.zip
!unravel/v2/beta-glucan.html.zip
!unravel/v2/host-glycan.html.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reproducibility framework — log dirs are noisy + per-machine; .npy decompressed
# sidecars (auto-decompressed by load_fasttext) are reconstituted on demand.
# Per-rep predictions/, leaderboard.csv, final_model.pkl, etc. ARE tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reproducibility/_*_logs/
reproducibility/_chain_logs/
reproducibility/rep_*/logs/
# Wakeup-pipeline stash backups (only useful locally for rollback)
artifacts/_passAB_backup_*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v2 tokenizer refinement (May 2026) — model bundles ARE shipped in-repo.
# The 6 v2 pkls (artifacts/final_model_v2.pkl + rep_*_v2/final_model.pkl) are
# joblib-saved with compress=("xz",6), shrinking them from 144 MB to ~20 MB each
# (~120 MB total). They are tracked via regular git (no LFS). joblib.load()
# auto-decompresses, so inference code does not change.
# Regenerate from scratch with:
#   python3 scripts/13_train_tc2_refinement.py        # → artifacts/final_model_v2.pkl
#   python3 scripts/13b_run_tc2_reproducibility.py    # → rep_*_v2/final_model.pkl
# Original deployed model (artifacts/final_model.pkl, rep_*/final_model.pkl)
# remains tracked via Git LFS and is the default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
